// Examples/TreasuryMandate/treasury-mandate.charter — End-to-end reference workload (`docs/rfc.md` §16, G3.7):
// Combines SHA-256 provenance (`G3.1`), `Power` competence (`G3.1`), 4-valued `Evidenced` custody
// confirmations + `Confidential` redaction + `Finding` adjudication (`G3.2`), stratified
// `Default`/`Exception` apparent authority (`G3.3`), dimensional `Money(USD, 2)` caps (`G3.4`),
// reporting deadlines (`T16`), revocation notice gaps (`T17`), non-imputation (`Law 3`), and
// intent-nonce idempotence (`Trace F`, `T09`, `T34`) across Traces A–F (§16.3).
//! explore: 1
//! explore-domain: usd-cents = 40000, 120000
Document MAIN "treasury-mandate.md" SHA256 "f6d8b3eba6d46f25f001a2aa0a2e7894471f53e40c8fcd3e724ac9de991633cc" Rank 1

Clause TM.1 In MAIN Approved "4417240bcfa07364a0e479bfb48114e950dc774662bc0e8bb84a873235e064ff"
  Text "A company may appoint an accountant to purchase approved bonds using a specified custody account up to the stated mandate cap. Any bond purchase beyond the mandate cap is not authorized on the company's behalf except where apparent authority protects an innocent counterparty without revocation notice."
  Norm "A company may appoint an accountant to purchase approved bonds using a specified custody account up to the stated mandate cap." => issue-mandate, revoke-mandate, deliver-revocation-notice
  Norm " Any bond purchase beyond the mandate cap is not authorized on the company's behalf except where apparent authority protects an innocent counterparty without revocation notice." => recognize-bond-purchase
Clause TM.2 In MAIN Approved "e57bd6a8ee6a34e5af1ce398b04bfb680c7e823bf55ae8cc57a6c852c6257dff"
  Text "An unauthorized purchase is recorded as an observed external event even when it has no authorized corporate effect. The accountant must submit a trade confirmation within two days of any observed purchase; a missing report breaches the reporting duty without establishing concealment or theft by the company unless the company directed the misconduct."
  Norm "An unauthorized purchase is recorded as an observed external event even when it has no authorized corporate effect." => execute-bond-trade
  Norm " The accountant must submit a trade confirmation within two days of any observed purchase; a missing report breaches the reporting duty without establishing concealment or theft by the company unless the company directed the misconduct." => submit-confirmation, report-trade-duty
Clause TM.3 In MAIN Approved "efb593fb4bac1b55b0f692d9daab01b7cb51c9f33c122349b1bf7d2809ea2af6"
  Text "Custody trade confirmation is evidenced by custodian and accountant filings; conflicting filings leave confirmation conflicted until an empowered audit panel issues a finding under the verified-receipt standard. Each purchase receipt and execution intent nonce may be recognized or settled at most once."
  Norm "Custody trade confirmation is evidenced by custodian and accountant filings; conflicting filings leave confirmation conflicted until an empowered audit panel issues a finding under the verified-receipt standard." => custodian-attest-receipt, accountant-dispute-receipt, adjudicate-receipt
  Norm " Each purchase receipt and execution intent nonce may be recognized or settled at most once." => settle-transfer-intent
Clause TM.4 In MAIN Approved "d48ec99db8055aa986feba9aa0aefae2983a5d9bbdefbc2455127d0c0a00c116"
  Text "Recognized corporate bond holdings stay within the mandate cap unless apparent authority applied prior to revocation notice, no purchase receipt or execution intent is settled twice, and independent delegate misconduct is never imputed to the company without company direction."
  Invariant "Recognized corporate bond holdings stay within the mandate cap unless apparent authority applied prior to revocation notice, " => mandate-authorization-bound
  Invariant "no purchase receipt or execution intent is settled twice, " => no-double-settlement
  Invariant "and independent delegate misconduct is never imputed to the company without company direction." => non-imputation-without-direction

// ---- Domains, dimensional Money(USD, 2), and state
Fact company Identified by AcmeCorp
Fact accountant Identified by CPA
Fact custodian Identified by CustodyBank
Fact counterparty Identified by Dealer1
Fact panel Identified by AuditPanel
Fact account Identified by CustAcctA
Fact asset Identified by Bond2028, UnapprovedNote
Fact trade-id Identified by T1, T2
Fact intent-id Identified by Intent1
Fact usd-cents Identified by Money(USD, 2)

Param report-window : Duration = 2
Param mandate-limit : Money(USD, 2) = 100000

Fact asset-approved Identified by asset
Fact account-permitted Identified by account
Fact mandate-active Identified by company * accountant
Fact mandate-revoked Identified by company * accountant
Fact revocation-notice Identified by counterparty
Fact panel-quorum Identified by panel
Fact apparent-authority-clause-granted Identified by company
Fact company-directed-trade Identified by trade-id * company

// Stratified Default/Exception rule for apparent-authority protection (§16.1, G3.3):
Fact apparent-authority-protects Identified by company * counterparty
  Default app-none Rejects when True
  Exception app-innocent Overrides app-none Holds when apparent-authority-clause-granted(company) && !revocation-notice(counterparty)

// Confidential 4-valued Evidenced custody receipt (§16.2, G3.2, T43):
Evidenced Fact custody-receipt-verified Identified by trade-id
  Confidential To auditor, panel

Function mandate-exposure Identified by company * usd-cents
Fact observed-trade Identified by trade-id * accountant * account * asset * counterparty * usd-cents
Fact trade-confirmed Identified by trade-id
Fact recognized-holding Identified by trade-id * company * asset * usd-cents
Fact recognized-via-apparent Identified by trade-id
Fact settled-intent Identified by intent-id * trade-id * usd-cents
Fact imputed-company-breach Identified by trade-id * company
  Holds when (Exists observed-trade:
    observed-trade.trade-id == trade-id
    && company-directed-trade(trade-id, company))

// ---- TM.1: Mandate appointment, revocation, and principal-binding recognition Power
Power issue-mandate Actor company Recipient accountant
  From TM.1 "A company may appoint an accountant to purchase approved bonds using a specified custody account up to the stated mandate cap."
  Holds when !mandate-active(company, accountant) && !mandate-revoked(company, accountant)
  Valid when !mandate-active(company, accountant) && !mandate-revoked(company, accountant)
  Creates mandate-active(company, accountant), mandate-exposure(company, usd-cents(0))

Power revoke-mandate Actor company Recipient accountant
  From TM.1 "A company may appoint an accountant to purchase approved bonds using a specified custody account up to the stated mandate cap."
  Holds when mandate-active(company, accountant)
  Valid when mandate-active(company, accountant)
  Creates mandate-revoked(company, accountant)
  Terminates mandate-active(company, accountant)

Act deliver-revocation-notice Actor company Recipient counterparty
  From TM.1 "A company may appoint an accountant to purchase approved bonds using a specified custody account up to the stated mandate cap."
  Holds when (Exists accountant: mandate-revoked(company, accountant))
  Creates revocation-notice(counterparty)

// ---- TM.2: External trade observation, 2-day reporting duty, and confirmation
Duty report-trade-duty Holder accountant Claimant company Related to trade-id
  From TM.2 "The accountant must submit a trade confirmation within two days of any observed purchase; a missing report breaches the reporting duty without establishing concealment or theft by the company unless the company directed the misconduct."
  Due within report-window

Physical execute-bond-trade Actor accountant Related to trade-id, account, asset, counterparty, usd-cents
  From TM.2 "An unauthorized purchase is recorded as an observed external event even when it has no authorized corporate effect."
  Creates observed-trade(trade-id, accountant, account, asset, counterparty, usd-cents)
        , report-trade-duty(accountant, AcmeCorp, trade-id)

Act submit-confirmation Actor accountant Related to trade-id
  From TM.2 "The accountant must submit a trade confirmation within two days of any observed purchase; a missing report breaches the reporting duty without establishing concealment or theft by the company unless the company directed the misconduct."
  Holds when (Exists observed-trade:
    observed-trade.trade-id == trade-id && observed-trade.accountant == accountant)
  Creates trade-confirmed(trade-id)
  Terminates report-trade-duty(accountant, AcmeCorp, trade-id)

// ---- TM.3: Evidenced custody attestations, Finding under `verifiedReceipt`, and idempotent settlement
Act custodian-attest-receipt Actor custodian Related to trade-id
  From TM.3 "Custody trade confirmation is evidenced by custodian and accountant filings; conflicting filings leave confirmation conflicted until an empowered audit panel issues a finding under the verified-receipt standard."
  Holds when (Exists observed-trade: observed-trade.trade-id == trade-id)
  Supports custody-receipt-verified(trade-id)

Act accountant-dispute-receipt Actor accountant Related to trade-id
  From TM.3 "Custody trade confirmation is evidenced by custodian and accountant filings; conflicting filings leave confirmation conflicted until an empowered audit panel issues a finding under the verified-receipt standard."
  Holds when (Exists observed-trade:
    observed-trade.trade-id == trade-id && observed-trade.accountant == accountant)
  Rebuts custody-receipt-verified(trade-id)

Finding adjudicate-receipt Actor panel Related to trade-id
  From TM.3 "Custody trade confirmation is evidenced by custodian and accountant filings; conflicting filings leave confirmation conflicted until an empowered audit panel issues a finding under the verified-receipt standard."
  Resolves custody-receipt-verified(trade-id)
  Standard verified-receipt
  Holds when Conflicted(custody-receipt-verified(trade-id)) || Unresolved(custody-receipt-verified(trade-id))
  Valid when panel-quorum(panel)

Power recognize-bond-purchase Actor custodian Related to trade-id, company, accountant, account, asset, counterparty, usd-cents
  From TM.1 "Any bond purchase beyond the mandate cap is not authorized on the company's behalf except where apparent authority protects an innocent counterparty without revocation notice."
  Holds when observed-trade(trade-id, accountant, account, asset, counterparty, usd-cents)
    && account-permitted(account) && asset-approved(asset)
    && custody-receipt-verified(trade-id)
    && !(Exists recognized-holding: recognized-holding.trade-id == trade-id)
  Valid when observed-trade(trade-id, accountant, account, asset, counterparty, usd-cents)
    && account-permitted(account) && asset-approved(asset)
    && custody-receipt-verified(trade-id)
    && !(Exists recognized-holding: recognized-holding.trade-id == trade-id)
    && ((mandate-active(company, accountant)
          && (Exists mandate-exposure:
                mandate-exposure.company == company
                && mandate-exposure.usd-cents + usd-cents <= mandate-limit))
        || apparent-authority-protects(company, counterparty))
  Creates recognized-holding(trade-id, company, asset, usd-cents)
        , (recognized-via-apparent(trade-id)
            When (!mandate-active(company, accountant)
                  || !(Exists mandate-exposure:
                         mandate-exposure.company == company
                         && mandate-exposure.usd-cents + usd-cents <= mandate-limit)))
        , (Foreach mandate-exposure:
            mandate-exposure(company, mandate-exposure.usd-cents + usd-cents)
            When mandate-exposure.company == company
              && mandate-active(company, accountant)
              && mandate-exposure.usd-cents + usd-cents <= mandate-limit)

Power settle-transfer-intent Actor custodian Related to intent-id, trade-id, company, asset, usd-cents
  From TM.3 "Each purchase receipt and execution intent nonce may be recognized or settled at most once."
  Holds when recognized-holding(trade-id, company, asset, usd-cents)
    && !(Exists settled-intent: settled-intent.intent-id == intent-id || settled-intent.trade-id == trade-id)
  Valid when recognized-holding(trade-id, company, asset, usd-cents)
    && !(Exists settled-intent: settled-intent.intent-id == intent-id || settled-intent.trade-id == trade-id)
  Creates settled-intent(intent-id, trade-id, usd-cents)

// ---- TM.4: Safety, accounting, and attribution Invariants (§16.4)
Invariant mandate-authorization-bound
  When (Forall mandate-exposure: mandate-exposure.usd-cents <= mandate-limit)
  From TM.4 "Recognized corporate bond holdings stay within the mandate cap unless apparent authority applied prior to revocation notice, "

Invariant no-double-settlement
  When (Forall settled-intent, settled-intent':
    settled-intent.trade-id == settled-intent'.trade-id && settled-intent.usd-cents == settled-intent'.usd-cents
    When settled-intent.intent-id == settled-intent'.intent-id)
  From TM.4 "no purchase receipt or execution intent is settled twice, "

Invariant non-imputation-without-direction
  When (Forall trade-id, company:
    company-directed-trade(trade-id, company) When imputed-company-breach(trade-id, company))
  From TM.4 "and independent delegate misconduct is never imputed to the company without company direction."
.

// ---- Genesis state
+account-permitted(CustAcctA).
+asset-approved(Bond2028).
issue-mandate(AcmeCorp, CPA).

// ---- Required Traces A–F (`docs/rfc.md` §16.3)

Scenario trace-a-normal-performance {
  // Principal issued mandate (cap 100,000 cents = $1,000.00); CPA buys Bond2028 for 40,000 cents:
  execute-bond-trade(CPA, T1, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  custodian-attest-receipt(CustodyBank, T1).
  ?Established(custody-receipt-verified(T1)).
  ?valid recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  ?recognized-holding(T1, AcmeCorp, Bond2028, 40000).
  ?mandate-exposure(AcmeCorp, 40000).
  submit-confirmation(CPA, T1).
  ?!violated report-trade-duty(CPA, AcmeCorp, T1).
}

Scenario trace-b-delegate-exceeds-scope {
  // CPA buys 120,000 cents (> 100,000 cap): physical event occurs; corporate recognition is void
  // unless apparent authority applies!
  execute-bond-trade(CPA, T1, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 120000).
  ?observed-trade(T1, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 120000).
  custodian-attest-receipt(CustodyBank, T1).
  ?!valid recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 120000).
  recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 120000).
  ?!recognized-holding(T1, AcmeCorp, Bond2028, 120000).
  // When separate apparent-authority clause is granted and Dealer1 had no revocation notice:
  +apparent-authority-clause-granted(AcmeCorp).
  ?apparent-authority-protects(AcmeCorp, Dealer1).
  ?valid recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 120000).
  recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 120000).
  ?recognized-holding(T1, AcmeCorp, Bond2028, 120000).
  ?recognized-via-apparent(T1).
  submit-confirmation(CPA, T1).
}

Scenario trace-c-missing-report-not-imputed-theft {
  // Trade occurs, CPA misses 2-day confirmation deadline -> reporting breach recorded,
  // WITHOUT inventing company concealment or imputing misconduct to AcmeCorp!
  execute-bond-trade(CPA, T1, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  @ 2.
  ?violated report-trade-duty(CPA, AcmeCorp, T1).
  ?!imputed-company-breach(T1, AcmeCorp).
  submit-confirmation(CPA, T1).
}

Scenario trace-d-conflicting-evidence-and-finding {
  // CustodyBank attests T1 while CPA disputes T1 -> Conflicted, recognition undetermined & void
  // until AuditPanel issues a valid Finding under `verifiedReceipt`!
  execute-bond-trade(CPA, T1, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  custodian-attest-receipt(CustodyBank, T1).
  accountant-dispute-receipt(CPA, T1).
  ?Conflicted(custody-receipt-verified(T1)).
  ?undetermined recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  ?!valid recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  +panel-quorum(AuditPanel).
  ?valid adjudicate-receipt(AuditPanel, T1).
  adjudicate-receipt(AuditPanel, T1).
  ?Established(custody-receipt-verified(T1)).
  ?valid recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  ?recognized-holding(T1, AcmeCorp, Bond2028, 40000).
  submit-confirmation(CPA, T1).
}

Scenario trace-e-revoked-mandate-and-notice-gap {
  // AcmeCorp revokes mandate; in the gap before Dealer1 receives notice, apparent authority governs;
  // once notice arrives, apparent authority terminates and further trades cannot bind AcmeCorp!
  +apparent-authority-clause-granted(AcmeCorp).
  revoke-mandate(AcmeCorp, CPA).
  execute-bond-trade(CPA, T1, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  custodian-attest-receipt(CustodyBank, T1).
  ?valid recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  submit-confirmation(CPA, T1).

  // Deliver revocation notice to Dealer1 -> T2 cannot bind AcmeCorp!
  deliver-revocation-notice(AcmeCorp, Dealer1).
  ?!apparent-authority-protects(AcmeCorp, Dealer1).
  execute-bond-trade(CPA, T2, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  custodian-attest-receipt(CustodyBank, T2).
  ?!valid recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T2, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  submit-confirmation(CPA, T2).
}

Scenario trace-f-idempotent-retry-prevents-double-transfer {
  // Retrying settlement with the same Intent1 nonce or for an already-settled trade T1 is void!
  execute-bond-trade(CPA, T1, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  custodian-attest-receipt(CustodyBank, T1).
  recognize-bond-purchase(CustodyBank, T1, AcmeCorp, CPA, CustAcctA, Bond2028, Dealer1, 40000).
  ?valid settle-transfer-intent(CustodyBank, Intent1, T1, AcmeCorp, Bond2028, 40000).
  settle-transfer-intent(CustodyBank, Intent1, T1, AcmeCorp, Bond2028, 40000).
  ?settled-intent(Intent1, T1, 40000).
  // Network timeout retry with same Intent1 nonce -> void (`!valid`), no second settlement!
  ?!valid settle-transfer-intent(CustodyBank, Intent1, T1, AcmeCorp, Bond2028, 40000).
  settle-transfer-intent(CustodyBank, Intent1, T1, AcmeCorp, Bond2028, 40000).
  submit-confirmation(CPA, T1).
}
